{"id":"n-20261014-8s3gzg","category":"business","display_title":"Dubi Amitai Leads Business Sector","display_title_he":"דובי אמיתי ממשיך להנהגת המגזר העסקי","short_summary":"Dubi Amitai has been unanimously elected to a third consecutive term as chairman of Israel's Presidium of the Business Sector, balancing economic leadership with extensive military reserve service.","english_level":"C1","words":436,"reading_time":3,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"Ynet","domain":"ynet.co.il","url":"https://www.ynet.co.il/economy/article/s1siqg3jfx","title":"דובי אמיתי נבחר לכהונה שלישית כיו”ר נשיאות המגזר העסקי","published_at":"2026-10-13T18:14:49.000Z"},{"name":"Walla","domain":"finance.walla.co.il","url":"https://finance.walla.co.il/item/3872001","title":"פותח קדנציה שלישית: דובי אמיתי נבחר פה אחד ליו\"ר נשיאות המגזר העסקי","published_at":"2026-10-13T12:37:00.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-13T12:37:00.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-14T06:10:11.483Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":8,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["Dubi Amitai has been unanimously elected to a third term as chairman of the Presidium of the Business Sector in Israel. Serving as the overarching umbrella organization for fourteen major economic sectors and industry groups, the Presidium represents a vast network of businesses ranging from manufacturing and commerce to banking, construction, hotels, insurance, agriculture, and independent entrepreneurship. In parallel to his extensive organizational duties, Amitai also heads the Farmers' Federation and is a fourth-generation native of the northern cooperative moshav of Metula, where he was born and continues to reside today.","Following his reelection, Amitai addressed the pressing challenges currently facing the national economy. According to his formal statements, the economic landscape must strategically shift away from prolonged crisis management toward active recovery, sustainable growth, increased productivity, and the restoration of much-needed certainty for both business owners and ordinary citizens. He highlighted that while politicians frequently direct their public messaging toward narrow partisan bases, the economic arena remains the primary space where shared societal interests genuinely intersect. The business sector has consistently demonstrated remarkable resilience and responsibility through three years of multi-front conflict, continuing to drive the economy forward under complex and demanding conditions.","Furthermore, Amitai stressed the vital importance of deepening international commercial connections with regional partners to prevent Israel from being sidelined during major diplomatic and economic developments currently taking shape across the area. Throughout the multi-front war that began on October 7, Amitai navigated a demanding dual reality. Alongside his continuous leadership of the business community, he served approximately six hundred days of military reserve duty in the northern sector as a lieutenant colonel and deputy brigade commander in Brigade 769, effectively bridging the gap between field demands and national economic policy. Operating from active reserve service, he worked persistently with the government, the Knesset, and key decision-makers to minimize commercial disruption.","During his previous tenure, the Presidium actively negotiated comprehensive compensation frameworks for impacted enterprises, established a northern national coordination headquarters in cooperation with the Ministry of Finance's Accountant General to channel governmental, philanthropic, and private investments, and advanced collective agreements protecting reserve soldiers and their spouses. Additionally, tireless advocacy efforts led to crucial legislative reforms requiring the state to indemnify employers by covering twenty percent of the social security contributions for employed reservists, thereby strengthening workplace protections.","Looking ahead, the leadership aims to continue easing regulatory burdens, opposing counterproductive tax increases that hinder development, and aligning professional training programs with actual market demands. Through initiatives like the \"Miloim 360\" employment desk and stronger global ties, the organization seeks to fortify the private sector as the primary engine driving national economic revitalization, investment, and employment."],"facts":[{"fact":"Dubi Amitai was elected unanimously for a third term as chairman of the Presidium of the Business Sector in Israel.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"The Presidium represents 14 economic organizations and industries in the country.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Amitai served approximately 600 days of reserve military duty on the northern front as a lieutenant colonel and deputy brigade commander since the outbreak of the war.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Amitai emphasized the need to transition the economy from crisis management to recovery, growth, and regional economic ties.","sources":[1,2]}],"glossary":[{"text":"Dubi Amitai","lemma":"Dubi Amitai","pos":"noun","he":"דובי אמיתי","name":"Dubi Amitai"},{"text":"unanimously","lemma":"unanimously","pos":"adverb","he":"פה אחד","name":""},{"text":"elected","lemma":"elect","pos":"verb","he":"נבחר","name":""},{"text":"third term","lemma":"third term","pos":"noun","he":"כהונה שלישית","name":""},{"text":"chairman","lemma":"chairman","pos":"noun","he":"יו״ר","name":""},{"text":"Presidium of the Business Sector","lemma":"Presidium of the Business Sector","pos":"noun","he":"נשיאות המגזר העסקי","name":"Presidium of the Business Sector"},{"text":"Israel","lemma":"Israel","pos":"noun","he":"ישראל","name":"Israel"},{"text":"overarching","lemma":"overarching","pos":"adjective","he":"כולל / ארגון גג","name":""},{"text":"umbrella organization","lemma":"umbrella organization","pos":"noun","he":"ארגון גג","name":""},{"text":"fourteen","lemma":"fourteen","pos":"number","he":"ארבעה עשר","name":""},{"text